HST PDF: an optional scanned signature and/or organisation seal image in the visible signature box.

The "Ký số" panel gets "Chèn ảnh chữ ký/con dấu" (off by default), "Ảnh chữ ký…", "Ảnh con dấu…"
with thumbnails, a layout choice ("Ảnh bên trái, chữ bên phải" by default, or "Ảnh phía trên, chữ
phía dưới") and "Không dùng ảnh". Choosing an image switches the option on. The choices and the file
URLs are kept only in the user profile (org.openoffice.Office.HSTPdfViewer/Signing); the images go
nowhere but into the PDFs the user signs.

- readSignatureImage: PNG (transparency kept) or JPEG; refuses files over 5 MB and, from the header
  before any decoding, images over 6000 pixels a side.
- createAppearance: the images keep their aspect ratio in at most 45 % of the box width on the left,
  or in its upper half; the text (layout B rules) shrinks into the rest. With both images the seal is
  printed over the left third of the signature, as on administrative documents (Nghị định 30/2020,
  Phụ lục I), the signature at 60 % of the seal's height. Each image is drawn once (one image
  XObject, its alpha as an SMask), reduced to 300 dpi at the drawn size.
- The default box grows with images to keep the text legible: 240 x 90 pt with the images on the
  left, 200 x 120 pt with them above. A box of a default size follows the image settings; one the
  user drew keeps its size.
- testSignatureImages: the limits, and a signature with both images that verifies and keeps /SMask.

